# Why V2 became padded

V2 was rejected. Its failure was geometric, not a missing material or texture.

1. `prepare_envelope` replaced the sleeve's two cross-section axes with one radius. It then added 9.5 mm and allowed up to 15 mm of outward movement. This rounded and inflated the forearm as well as filling the elbow notch.
2. The centreline was two straight segments joined at the elbow. It did not provide a continuous cloth station through the bend. The scalar radial envelope therefore treated the joint as two joined tubes.
3. The corrective smoothed the deformed patch and pushed it outward to a minimum skin clearance. It did not preserve material edge lengths. The largest inverse-skinned morph move reached 48.7 mm in rest coordinates.
4. The 3.6 mm inner-fold treatment was much smaller than that broad expansion. Adding more grooves would not have corrected the padded construction.
5. Native skin weights vary strongly around an elbow section. At the measured rest elbow station, lower-arm weight spans about 0.25–0.91. The coat inherits that uneven muscle/skin crease, although a sleeve's material should transition more evenly along its length.

