## Specific V3 experiment

V3 keeps the connected coat mesh and sewn boundaries. It does not need a new open panel or another collar join.

- Use a continuous curved centreline through the elbow.
- Keep separate front/back and transverse ellipse axes. Smooth the small local shape irregularities without adding a fixed radial allowance. Limit target section growth and permit small inward as well as outward cloth moves.
- Reassign only the interior sleeve's upper/lower-arm blend by longitudinal cloth rows. Preserve the total native-arm influence and taper to the unchanged shoulder and cuff weights.
- Bake one elbow-angle corrective with rest-edge stretch constraints and weak bending constraints. Keep the outer elbow extended, and let the inner material compress into shallow oblique folds.
- Use actual local crossings and a multi-ray body-volume check for collision diagnosis. Do not treat one nearest normal as proof of being inside.

This is a testable construction change. It is not yet accepted. Review the same four actual exported poses, actual surface crossings, section areas and remaining edge stretch before deciding whether to proceed. No shared source or assets are changed.
